#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054554 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e77fe2f6-0e93-5378-aa8d-cc6d5122bdaa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function With Common Factors"}] :question/id #uuid "f4a45939-a80c-5e3e-bf2f-b3097a42c2ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-5137" :question/problem "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x+1}{x^2-x-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+1}{{x}^{2}-x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+1}{(x+1)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x+1)}}{\\cancel{(x+1)}(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the numerator equal to zero, we get $1=0,$ which is a false statement. Therefore, $f(x)=0$ has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054555 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d98f7bd-2351-5eb8-80ff-67adcba4adbc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function With a Quadratic Numerator and No Common Factors"}] :question/id #uuid "bf127b16-01c5-58c9-903a-e00fe349c011" :question/math-academy-id "e-5139" :question/problem "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x^2-4x}{x^2+5x+6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x}{{x}^{2}+5x+6} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(x-4)}{(x+2)(x+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(x)=0$ are $x=0$ and $x=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054556 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "688b4f72-387b-5757-9b81-d24a1d9c727d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function Containing a Cubic Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "6d6b343f-756f-5d3b-9231-fe7796d85653" :question/math-academy-id "e-5142" :question/problem "Solve $f(x)=0$, where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x^3-2x^2-9x+18}{x^2-x-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}{{x}^{2}-x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x-2)-9(x-2)}{(x-2)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)({x}^{2}-9)}{(x-2)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)(x-3)(x+3)}{(x-2)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x-3)(x+3)}{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the numerator equal to zero and solving for $x$ gives\n\n$$\n(x-3)(x+3) = 0 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x = \\pm3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(x)=0$ are $x=3$ and $x=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054566 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d084b4e-7ca3-5569-b2a5-42c4b8f47917" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function With a Linear Numerator and No Common Factors"}] :question/id #uuid "b8371b7c-dfd8-52b3-9c34-00d6814cc5de" :question/math-academy-id "e-5257" :question/problem "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{2x + 1}{x^2 + x - 6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+1}{(x+3)(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d084b4e-7ca3-5569-b2a5-42c4b8f47917" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function With a Linear Numerator and No Common Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b375d78-a87f-59d3-9572-b17e9d856299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515040} {:answer/id #uuid "53cf8488-82bd-5c40-a7af-14f82f5ba4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The equation has no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515055} {:answer/id #uuid "54bdfb8e-a045-5d76-b2e2-d543a6fcf2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515062} {:answer/id #uuid "849f979a-f3f5-53e7-b5cd-260cb22f029e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515145} {:answer/id #uuid "ef848463-b168-563e-9883-b757267bfe81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "849f979a-f3f5-53e7-b5cd-260cb22f029e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515145} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcea6cf5-7717-5f7d-aee1-c92728386a3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2cc15c9-6ca6-5c2d-9f16-f12bfe047553" :question/math-academy-id "q-113062" :question/problem "Solve $f(x)=0$ where $f(x)=\\frac{x+5}{2{x}^{2}-5x-25}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+5}{2{x}^{2}-5x-25} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+5}{(x-5)(2x+5)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5 & =0 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e77fe2f6-0e93-5378-aa8d-cc6d5122bdaa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function With Common Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08bdec83-c6ad-5c2f-8191-80fcaec9c8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No roots" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514889} {:answer/id #uuid "43ee574a-8a30-5b2a-b163-e85baed477ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515018} {:answer/id #uuid "784e53da-ac7d-5028-9968-a4631f4feaf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=0,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515120} {:answer/id #uuid "7855cd61-3ce4-59af-aa08-15f52848df6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515123} {:answer/id #uuid "8c0ac787-d0ae-5c5f-8b63-b275aac416bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=-4,-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7855cd61-3ce4-59af-aa08-15f52848df6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515123} :answer-field/id #uuid "a18f4ead-179e-5865-b01c-c77ce604e10d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60c93613-0dc8-54aa-a9e0-7ec27315eb60" :question/math-academy-id "q-113088" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(z)=\\frac{{z}^{2}+5z+4}{{z}^{2}+4z}.$" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(z)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(z)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{z}^{2}+5z+4}{{z}^{2}+4z}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(z) & =\\frac{{z}^{2}+5z+4}{{z}^{2}+4z} \\\\  & =\\frac{(z+1)(z+4)}{z(z+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(z+1)\\cancel{(z+4)}}{z\\cancel{(z+4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(z+1)}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+1 & =0\\,⟹\\,z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(z)=0$ is $z=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "688b4f72-387b-5757-9b81-d24a1d9c727d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function Containing a Cubic Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0212f041-3e0f-56b5-9183-937e4d9b010f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514876} {:answer/id #uuid "1c681bc2-db89-5b8b-a888-6e454a854953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514934} {:answer/id #uuid "cef1acc7-0b8d-5cee-81e8-42810d42b824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515306} {:answer/id #uuid "d52afbe6-85e4-50b9-9547-01474e5a8221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515320} {:answer/id #uuid "f109c122-ed91-5e73-a873-73bb3ed90155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c681bc2-db89-5b8b-a888-6e454a854953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514934} :answer-field/id #uuid "85571c32-e16c-59f6-ab7a-5ad637ae9027" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c9052e44-409b-5493-8da2-7b4975b14835" :question/math-academy-id "q-25299" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-20}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}.$" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-20}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-20}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-4)}{{x}^{2}(x-2)-9(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-4)}{({x}^{2}-9)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-4)}{(x+3)(x-3)(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)(x-4)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-5,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ are $x=-5$ and $x=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d98f7bd-2351-5eb8-80ff-67adcba4adbc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function With a Quadratic Numerator and No Common Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "377800ac-d02d-5ee7-9054-9beacb06ab2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=-1,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514993} {:answer/id #uuid "4df9e14b-ce47-5984-8b22-2b57b89d6d13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=-3,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515044} {:answer/id #uuid "6b18dd16-63d0-56e3-a6ab-4af8268e8f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=-2,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515094} {:answer/id #uuid "9e873323-4894-55fb-b9e3-3c4721bcb462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=-1,\\,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515207} {:answer/id #uuid "f2919458-4ec2-5e45-beec-98e5b60984fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No real roots" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "377800ac-d02d-5ee7-9054-9beacb06ab2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=-1,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514993} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0ef1040-77da-560a-87d7-15632abbe381" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19bba278-dfe5-5c03-8d05-5a3c3649901e" :question/math-academy-id "q-25301" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(w)=\\frac{{w}^{2}-w-2}{w-5}.$" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(w)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(w)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{w}^{2}-w-2}{w-5}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor $f(w),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(w) & =\\frac{{w}^{2}-w-2}{w-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{(w-2)(w+1)}{w-5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $w:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(w-2)(w+1) & =0 \\\\ w & =-1,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(w)=0$ are $w=-1$ and $w=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515608 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "688b4f72-387b-5757-9b81-d24a1d9c727d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function Containing a Cubic Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77453159-e112-56b2-8504-5b0644f70b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515116} {:answer/id #uuid "8ebd7bf8-010c-5124-aefb-f8446638f67b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515172} {:answer/id #uuid "d2473aef-b55a-5e58-afc4-eed2722a8015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515313} {:answer/id #uuid "e3e0ad3e-39e3-5115-b2ac-b21b4654024e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515347} {:answer/id #uuid "ea763d4b-09e3-5e5c-b191-0925974ea72f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3e0ad3e-39e3-5115-b2ac-b21b4654024e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515347} :answer-field/id #uuid "6467ad98-5aba-5b91-be20-bcc574e8fa7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ddd618d8-1530-59f2-b97b-98d26b79c22a" :question/math-academy-id "q-25307" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x-10}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}.$" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x-10}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x-10}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{{x}^{2}(x-2)-9(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{({x}^{2}-9)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(x-2)}{(x+3)(x-3)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)\\cancel{(x-2)}}{(x+3)(x-3)\\cancel{(x-2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)}{(x+3)(x-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5=0\\,⟹\\,x=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "688b4f72-387b-5757-9b81-d24a1d9c727d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function Containing a Cubic Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cb3ffc0-7e51-564d-b7d4-590f967566e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=-5,\\,-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514899} {:answer/id #uuid "235c68a8-d1a1-5979-b0d4-01b41af330ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514955} {:answer/id #uuid "3d6c5120-1dd4-5bd1-8211-11cd0fdf9e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515004} {:answer/id #uuid "48b461e7-6fb0-560a-8a73-95106caf3b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515028} {:answer/id #uuid "84c1c219-bfe2-5e58-a44f-84da5210e4da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=4,\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48b461e7-6fb0-560a-8a73-95106caf3b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515028} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfc3d8a5-cbd4-5701-af7e-3598dbd3e3f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88464372-728b-5e12-ab3a-004869808716" :question/math-academy-id "q-25312" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(h)=\\frac{{h}^{2}+9h+20}{{h}^{3}+3{h}^{2}-25h-75}.$" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(h)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(h)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{h}^{2}+9h+20}{{h}^{3}+3{h}^{2}-25h-75}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(h) & =\\frac{{h}^{2}+9h+20}{{h}^{3}+3{h}^{2}-25h-75} \\\\  & =\\frac{(h+5)(h+4)}{{h}^{2}(h+3)-25(h+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(h+5)(h+4)}{({h}^{2}-25)(h+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(h+5)(h+4)}{(h+5)(h-5)(h+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(h+5)}(h+4)}{\\cancel{(h+5)}(h-5)(h+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{h+4}{(h-5)(h+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h+4=0\\,⟹\\,h=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(h)=0$ is $h=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e77fe2f6-0e93-5378-aa8d-cc6d5122bdaa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function With Common Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "637f3eea-aba7-5bc5-b49d-12225df44666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "637f3eea-aba7-5bc5-b49d-12225df44666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515086} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7fb947e-e267-5840-8345-72d0ea80120c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35ce6eb4-991f-5d5d-bf8d-bb7ed13aec66" :question/math-academy-id "q-270847" :question/problem "Find the roots of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+14}{{x}^{2}-4}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+14}{{x}^{2}-4}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+14}{{x}^{2}-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-7)(x-2)}{(x+2)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-7)\\cancel{(x-2)}}{(x+2)\\cancel{(x-2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-7}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-7 & =0\\,⟹\\,x=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515617 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d98f7bd-2351-5eb8-80ff-67adcba4adbc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function With a Quadratic Numerator and No Common Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceeefb89-cfe9-5b37-9bbc-39109065eb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceeefb89-cfe9-5b37-9bbc-39109065eb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515305} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f6715e4-b16a-58f4-9041-8f3d0e03cf18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515449} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f31b0c1-0fac-5fda-9fee-b63a90c2d43a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f31b0c1-0fac-5fda-9fee-b63a90c2d43a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514976} :answer-field/id #uuid "78c8b077-e976-516b-8732-4f6c3a8a52fe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f03d8bec-d8c1-5f5b-8e78-5d11e09f4352" :question/math-academy-id "q-277862" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the roots of $g(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-16}{{x}^{2}-7x+10}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$\nand\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $g(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $g(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-16}{{x}^{2}-7x+10}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor $g(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-16}{{x}^{2}-7x+10} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+4)(x-4)}{(x-2)(x-5)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =-4,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $g(x)=0$, in ascending order, are $x=-4$ and $x=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "688b4f72-387b-5757-9b81-d24a1d9c727d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function Containing a Cubic Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb061fbc-28bf-5b2a-84b8-eec238396424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb061fbc-28bf-5b2a-84b8-eec238396424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515397} :answer-field/id #uuid "2090e862-943c-54e8-bc45-27edfeefbaac" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515421} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9be7cb15-5f79-511e-9d04-e09b5b217932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9be7cb15-5f79-511e-9d04-e09b5b217932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515202} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4543e63-f861-5762-bec4-80e1b6d0937b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8460a1ed-5635-5121-961a-4a208d9777ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-278034" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the roots of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x+2}{3x-3}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$\nand\n$\\,\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The roots of $f(x)$ are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x+2}{3x-3}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x+2}{3x-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x-2)-1(x-2)}{3x-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)(x-2)}{3(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-1)(x+1)(x-2)}{3(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-1)}(x+1)(x-2)}{3\\cancel{(x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+1)(x-2)}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,\\,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(x)=0$, in ascending order, are $x=-1$ and $x=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d084b4e-7ca3-5569-b2a5-42c4b8f47917" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Rational Function With a Linear Numerator and No Common Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "167d4b9b-b6e5-52dc-b8f7-bf49a917fdb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514920} {:answer/id #uuid "862a142c-3d12-5829-8961-607a133af512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The equation has no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515153} {:answer/id #uuid "8f557bac-7bbb-5a6b-9ece-8401b03a9e75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515177} {:answer/id #uuid "af1622c7-40b8-5bd4-8e78-9857f18ace03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515240} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b1d9a3-0101-5ff1-aa74-6f16ed44bf13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af1622c7-40b8-5bd4-8e78-9857f18ace03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515240} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d83edb1-1f8c-5230-883b-d0994ae0440d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd3c4104-b695-59fd-871c-afa5ad204e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-70499" :question/problem "Solve $f(t)=0$ where $f(t)=\\frac{t-3}{{t}^{2}+6t+5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $f(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\frac{t-3}{{t}^{2}+6t+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{t-3}{(t+5)(t+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-3 & =0 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(t)=0$ is $t=3.$"}]}
